      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Going in I understood that you can only have 2 of the 3;- price- performance- quality.I had done some research before hand and wanted to go with and expensive LG panels and SolarEdge Inverter and optimisers. J&M talked me through the pro's and con's and were actually trying to down sell me. In the end I compromised and agreed that JA 290W panels with SolarEdge inverter and optimisers provided the best compromise.The installers were top notch, kept me in the loop all the way and answered any questions I had. They had a little problem with the LAN cable, and although had to come back twice to fix it, it was sorted within 1.5 weeks. This was not a big deal as they had the wifi working.I didn't share quote information between the vendors, yet like for like they came out way cheaper then anyone else (by about $500 - $1500 depending on what system you asked for).",
